2:T621,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does a kitchen renovation cost in Watford?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough typical UK guide, a refresh may cost around £3,000–£8,000, a like-for-like replacement around £8,000–£18,000, and a full renovation with layout changes around £15,000–£30,000 or more. Every project differs, so request a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is usually included in a kitchen fitting quote?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It may include cabinet installation, worktops, appliances, plumbing, electrical work, tiling, flooring, removal and waste, but inclusions vary. Request an itemised quotation and check whether VAT and preparation work are included."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it cheaper to keep the same kitchen layout?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Keeping water, waste, cooking and electrical points in similar positions can reduce the work required for service connections. Any saving will depend on the existing condition of the room and the products being installed."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much contingency should I allow for a kitchen renovation?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Consider allowing a contingency for unforeseen work, especially in older properties or where the condition behind existing units is unknown. Possible issues can include hidden leaks, uneven floors, damaged walls or changes to the specification."}}]}7:["slug","kitchen-renovation-cost-watford","d"]
